io","poi_name":"Turkey foot","subject":"Tim from ohio","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13431","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13431"}},{"id":"13432","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3028","description":"","caption":"Tim 1","poi_name":"turkeyfoot","subject":"Tim from Ohio","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13432","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13432"}},{"id":"13433","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3028","description":"","caption":"back surf","poi_name":"Turkeyfoot","subject":"Tim from Ohio","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13433","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13433"}},{"id":"1486","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3029","description":"Brian backing down to get on the wave","caption":"Like father like son","poi_name":"Turkey foot","subject":"Brian and Jay Koontz","author":"Jeff Totten","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1486","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1486"}},{"id":"1487","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3029","description":"All alone near the bottom of Turkey foot","caption":"Nice ride","poi_name":"Turkey foot","subject":"  Jay Koontz","author":"Jeff Totten","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1487","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1487"}},{"id":"1488","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3029","description":"Dein on the last wave.","caption":"Smile","poi_name":"Turkey foot","subject":"Dein Higgins","author":"Jeff Totten","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1488","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1488"}}],"detail":{"id":"1472","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"**Maumee Rapids**\n\n* * *\n\n[![](/photos/archive/13432.jpeg)](/photos/?photoid=13432)\n\nThis is a big wide river with small ledge type rapids and very few eddys. There are some nice surfing waves and a few side surfing holes. From the put in it starts out flat with **Missionary Island** on the right , when you get to the end of the Island go river right for some warm up surf waves.\n\nJust down stream is **Roche de Bout rapids**, go river left of a big rock with a good wave, good eddy here.\n\nNext Island run river left for what Tim Staley calls M **illion Dollar Wave**, a river wide wave.\n\nWatch for a nice play wave/hole on the far left by some big houses .\n\nThe biggest rapid T **urkey Foot** comes at the end of the run ,just up stream of the I- 475 bridge. You can park and play at this rapid with out a shuttle.The waves/holes can get fairly big and at 6500 the current is strong with no eddys.\n\n[![](/photos/archive/13435.jpeg)](/photos/?photoid=13435)\n\nWatch out for the fisherman on this run. It is a popular spot in the spring and they wade out in the river to fish. At the higher flows they can't get out as far so there is more room to paddle. I went there one time and the water was good but too many fisherman to paddle.\n\n* * *\n\nIf you have any info that you would like to add please [e-mail](mailto:joyce@juno.com) me and I will add it to this page.\n\nThe [Sandusky River](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1478/) is fun and only 30 min. away.\n\nThe [Upper Sandusky River at Tiffin](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/1477/) is only 45 min. away and can be fun too.\n\n* * *","averageGradient":"9","maxGradient":"15","length":"10.7","correlations":[{"reachID":"1472","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"4000","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"10000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"Maumee River at Waterville OH","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"04193500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"4880","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.97","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"41.5000526","longitude":"-83.7127145"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/04193500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/04193500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"4880","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["109724","114977"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-83.78724618038547,41.44676820233303],[-83.78682991371943,41.44700600233267],[-83.78535531372172,41.44784826899803],[-83.78363751372439,41.447936068997876],[-83.78320558039172,41.44818280233085],[-83.78288111372558,41.44836820233053],[-83.78250291372615,41.44858420233021],[-83.78245958039287,41.44883226899651],[-83.78151411372767,41.44937226899566],[-83.77949311373085,41.45119666899279],[-83.77935738039771,41.45294940232344],[-83.78024238039632,41.455682668985844],[-83.78031751372953,41.45720340231686],[-83.7797761137304,41.46030460231202],[-83.77851131373234,41.4616968689765],[-83.77699818040134,41.462560868975174],[-83.7741233804058,41.46342066897387],[-83.7674239804162,41.46277860230816],[-83.7672715137498,41.46270260230